# Privacy and security

- Precise GPS coordinates stay in the browser. Server requests may contain only
  the existing coarse geohash or a city slug.
- Favorites and saved places remain device-local in IndexedDB unless the user
  explicitly approves a product change.
- All admin and cron mutations must fail closed in production and retain their
  route-level authorization checks.
- Validate user-supplied feed URLs through `src/lib/url-security.ts`; preserve
  HTTPS-only and private-network protections across redirects and DNS results.
- Never print, commit, snapshot, or expose values from `.env*`. Tests use
  obvious non-secret placeholders and restore changed environment variables.
- Opening the map is the user-controlled boundary for requests to OpenFreeMap.
- Live database audits use staging infrastructure. Pull-request tests must not
  mutate shared Neon branches.
